# Walkthrough: PM Finance Tracking & Workflow Automation Integration

I've completed the implementation of your PM Finance Tracking feature in the TDGAMES_App, as well as the 2-way Slack Auto-Threading Sync from ClickUp.

Here's an overview of the new additions and achieved results:

### Custom Name Mappings
A custom UI mapping tab allows mapping original user display names (e.g. `user123`) from Slack/Discord/ClickUp into unified human-readable job titles or customized names for the synced message.

### List Auto-Threading Mappings
You can now map specific ClickUp Lists to specific Slack Channels natively from the Web UI!

- **Configurable Lists**: Open the **List Configs** tab to manage rules.
- **Routing**: Define `List ID` ➔ `Channel ID`.
- **Review Routing**: Provide raw `<@U...>` tagging strings for the Slack user that should be pinged when a task moves to `CLIENT_REVIEW`.
- **Relationship Integrity**: Maps are strictly bound to existing Customers and Projects for clear data segregation across the dashboard.
- Features real-time setup without requiring a database admin to touch NocoDB. 

## Completed Features

### 1. NocoDB Finance Tracking Database Structure
- Created a `PM_Tasks_Tracking` table in your NocoDB instance directly connected to your [.env](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/.env) configuration.
- Successfully imported the following fields: 
  - `Task_ID` (ClickUp ID string, serves as external ID link)
  - `Task_Name` 
  - `Job_Type` (Auto-mapped as either `Art` or `Animation` based on list parameters)
  - [Status](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/platforms/clickup-api.js#94-103)
  - `Assignee` 
  - `Task_URL`
- NocoDB internal fields (Hidden from ClickUp):
  - `Cost` (decimal data type, formatted in USD)
  - `Currency` (dropdown selector for USD/VND)
  - `Payment_Status` (Options: Unpaid, Advance Paid, Fully Paid)
  - `Notes` 

### 2. External Data Flow: ClickUp ➔ NocoDB Sync
- Extended your existing [public/index.html](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/index.html) webhook server file inside [src/webhooks/clickup.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/webhooks/clickup.js) to process Task lifecycle events: `taskCreated`, `taskUpdated`, and `taskDeleted`.
- Filtered hooks automatically to sync exclusively from the `Art` and `Animation` folder structures.
- Implemented smart Upserts inside [src/nocodb.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/nocodb.js) to overwrite basic details seamlessly from ClickUp without destroying or overriding localized financial information. 
   > [!TIP]
   > Changing a task's name or Assignee from ClickUp will automatically reflect over to the NocoDB Dashboard while ensuring your financial data is fully preserved.

### 3. Integrated Custom User Interface for the PM Team
- Deployed a **PM Finance Tracking** navigation tab to the root `http://localhost:3000` view panel ([public/index.html](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/index.html)).
- Inserted two dynamic `<select>` dropdown menus for rapid pipeline filtering via **Job_Type** and **Payment_Status**.
- Designed a native modal editing window inside [public/app.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/app.js) and [src/api.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/api.js) for quick inline overrides:
  - Can apply *Cost (USD/VND)* directly from the modal.
  - Can switch states between *Unpaid*, *Advance Paid*, and *Fully Paid* directly from the **table view** via inline dropdown menus (no modal needed).
  - Can input rich internal *Notes* from the modal.
  - *Task Status* is preserved as a **read-only** field, ensuring the source of truth for workflow statuses remains strictly in ClickUp.

## Instructions / Testing Validation

1. Access the web dashboard locally (Ensure nodemon `npm run dev` is running).
2. Click on the brand new **💰 PM Tracking** sidebar element.
3. Your active Clickup tasks should map successfully. Try opening ClickUp entirely outside of NocoDB to update a task's title or status. You will see the update in this window reflected with preserved custom cost metrics.
4. Attempt clicking **✏️ Edit (Local)** on any task within the UI to simulate PM adjustments: Input a cost, change payment-type, or modify internal notes. Observe that the actual "Task Status" is read-only.
5. Click on **🔗 List Configs** to add Auto-Thread Sync mappings from ClickUp to Slack. Make sure to input the precise ClickUp List ID, Channel ID, and the raw User Ping string.

### 4. Custom Review Tags & 24h Reminders
- **Dynamic Tagging**: When a ClickUp task enters `CLIENT_REVIEW` status, the Bot will send a Slack message using the exact, raw text you provided in the **Users to Tag (Review)** field on the List Configs web UI. For example, if you input `<@U08DZ4GTPBP> please review`, the bot will output exactly that string to ping the user.
- **24h Auto-Reminders**: A new cron job scans active lists every 30 minutes for tasks that have been untouched in `CLIENT_REVIEW` for longer than 24 hours. When found, it automatically posts that exact custom payload string into the corresponding Slack thread. Tasks are guaranteed to only be reminded once per 24 hours.

